1785467561961883	skills-dev	itc:v3:AWLJk_5k8kmTJEAAAAAAQda_7XqtagAAAAEwAQ		item.create	bn-2eg	{"description":"The submission key is dropped when it rides along in the same write as the text.\n\nReproduced against codex (v0.146.0) in a 200x50 vessel agent:\n\n    vessel spawn --name probe --rows 50 --cols 200 --cwd DIR -- codex\n    vessel send probe 'Reply with exactly ENTER_TEST.' --enter\n    # 6s later: text sits in the composer, unsubmitted\n\n    vessel send-keys probe enter\n    # submits immediately, agent answers\n\n--newline (LF) fails identically to --enter (CR), so this is not key encoding.\nThe distinguishing factor is that the key arrives in the same write as the text:\ndelivering it as a separate call, after a short pause, works every time.\n\nLikely cause: the TUI applies timing-based paste detection, and a trailing\nCR/LF inside what looks like one pasted burst is treated as content rather than\nas a keypress. Same reasoning as bracketed paste.\n\nImpact: --enter is the documented ergonomic path for driving an interactive\nagent, and it silently does nothing for the main class of program vessel exists\nto drive. The failure is silent -- the prompt looks delivered.\n\nPossible fixes: flush the text and delay a beat before the key, send the key as\na separate PTY write, or document that --enter is unsafe for TUIs and point at\nsend-keys.","kind":"bug","size":"s","title":"send --enter and --newline do not submit to TUI agents"}	blake3:wJ8ZE23_xB1IECVvTcsJegUJgW0ESgMx7nxxtcjO-qQ
1785467572380728	skills-dev	itc:v3:AWLJk_5k8kmTJEAAAAAAQda_7XqtagAAAAEwAg		item.create	bn-1a0f	{"description":"Sending a multi-line prompt to a TUI agent currently requires hand-rolling\nbracketed paste through send-bytes:\n\n    1b5b3230307e + <utf-8 text as hex> + 1b5b3230317e     # ESC[200~ .. ESC[201~\n\nWithout it, the first newline submits a truncated prompt and every remaining\nline lands as its own turn -- three separate agent turns for one prompt, each\nbilled, none of them what was asked.\n\nVerified working: wrapped that way, a three-line prompt lands in codex's\ncomposer as three lines, unsubmitted, and then submits as a single turn.\n\nProposal: 'vessel send ID --paste TEXT' (or --bracketed) that wraps the payload\nin the paste markers. Reading the text from stdin with '-' would help too;\nprompts for coding agents are routinely long enough to be awkward as argv.\n\nThis is the single most common thing an orchestrator needs and the most\nerror-prone to reproduce by hand, since the failure is silent and looks like the\nagent misunderstood the prompt.","kind":"task","size":"s","title":"Add bracketed-paste mode to send, for multi-line prompts"}	blake3:C2RP45CX5tvoAyQnKAM-_LNZwvnY1e5MRg1_kf0W-IY
